  "result": "I've graded submission s2 for quiz 0001 and written the grades to `grades/0001-s2.json`. The score is 3 correct, 2 partial and 1 wrong.\n\n- **Correct:**\n  - q1: you picked the loop as what makes an agent.\n  - q2: you saw that the model outputs a tool request rather than running anything.\n  - q5: you said the result goes back as the next input so the model can decide its next step.\n- **Partial:**\n  - q4: your answer of 4 is right, but your reasoning said the model runs the tools itself (M4). The program runs them between model calls.\n  - q6: you said the model picks a tool by its name. It actually uses the full description, meaning what the tool does and its parameters.\n- **Wrong:**\n  - q3: you chose \"left to run longer, it will eventually fix the bug\". That is M6, the belief that an agent needs no stopping condition. With the same failure repeating 40 times, every new step sees the same input, so only a step limit stops it and caps cost.\n\n**Next step:** redo q4 in writing. For each of the 4 model calls, note what the model outputs and what the program does before the next call. Then write a full description (purpose and parameters) for `check_calendar`.\n\nI also added `learning-records/0003-loop-structure-and-stopping.md` and updated `NOTES.md` with the open misconceptions and the q6 gap.",
